cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dmsa: Directional Methylation Set Analysis"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ein-Dor
    given-names: Tsachi
    email: teindor@runi.ac.il
    affiliation: "Reichman University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3078-7591"
version: 1.20.2
date-released: 2026-08-21
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/teindor/dmsa"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22023957"
    description: "Concept DOI - resolves to the latest release. Cite this one."
abstract: >-
  DMSA aligns probe-level DNA methylation effects to their predicted
  consequence for gene expression before aggregating them, tests each unit
  through three pre-specified lenses on one permutation stream, and names the
  responsible gene inside level-local families with family-wise error control.
keywords:
  - DNA methylation
  - gene set analysis
  - epigenome-wide association
  - multiple testing
  - permutation inference
